# System Architecture

## Core Modules

1. Authentication & Security
2. Property Management
3. Building Management
4. Unit Management
5. Tenant Management
6. Lease Management
7. Rent Collection
8. Wallet & Finance
9. Utility Billing
10. Service Charge Management
11. Maintenance & Repairs
12. Vendor Management
13. Visitor Management
14. Documents Management
15. Notification Engine
16. Reporting & Analytics
17. Audit & Compliance
18. User & Role Management
19. Mobile Applications
20. Support & Knowledge Base

## Design Principles

- API-first design with versioned REST and GraphQL endpoints
- Tenant-aware security for strong data isolation
- Role-based access control with fine-grained permission assignments
- Mobile-first workflows and responsive web experiences
- Modular, extensible architecture for future feature expansion
- Auditability, compliance, and multi-jurisdiction support
- Observability and operational transparency

---

# Multi-Tenant Architecture

The platform shall support:

## Option 1: Single Owner

One landlord managing one or many buildings.

## Option 2: Property Management Company

A property management company managing dozens or hundreds of properties for multiple owners.

## Option 3: Enterprise Estate Management

Managing multiple estates and properties across cities, regions, and countries.

### Data Isolation

- Tenant-aware data partitioning by tenant ID, property, portfolio, or business unit
- Logical separation for shared services, settings, and configuration
- Per-tenant security controls and access policies
- Scoped admin and owner portals for secure cross-property management

---

# RBAC (Role Based Access Control)

## Dynamic Role Management

Administrators must be able to:

- Create roles
- Edit roles
- Clone roles
- Disable roles
- Archive roles
- Restore archived roles

## Permission Categories

### Property Permissions

- Create Property
- Edit Property
- Delete Property
- View Property
- Manage Property Settings

### Unit Permissions

- Create Units
- Edit Units
- Transfer Units
- Lock Units
- View Unit Status

### Lease Permissions

- Create Lease
- Approve Lease
- Renew Lease
- Amend Lease
- Terminate Lease
- View Lease Documents

### Financial Permissions

- View Revenue
- View Expenses
- Approve Expenses
- Reverse Payments
- Refund Payments
- Manage Budgets
- View Ledgers

### Maintenance Permissions

- Create Requests
- Assign Requests
- Approve Requests
- Close Requests
- Manage Work Orders

### Reports Permissions

- View Reports
- Export Reports
- Schedule Reports

### Administration Permissions

- User Management
- Role Management
- System Configuration
- Tenant Configuration
- Audit Access

### Additional Permission Areas

- Notification Management
- Document Management
- Visitor Access Control
- Utility & Billing Management
- Vendor & Supplier Access
- Support & Ticketing
- Mobile / USSD Access
- Integrations Management

## Permission Rules

- Permissions should be assignable at tenant, property, building, unit, and portfolio scope
- Support granular actions (Create, Read, Update, Delete, Approve, Export, Publish, Archive, Manage)
- Enable hierarchical role inheritance, role groups, and permission overrides
- Allow custom permission labels and composite permission bundles
- Enforce separation of duties and dual approval for sensitive operations
- Support time-based access windows and temporary role assignments
- Maintain audit history for role changes and approval workflows

---

# Property Classification Framework

## Property Categories

Every property must belong to one primary category before creation:

1. Residential
2. Commercial

## Residential Property Types

Administrators should be able to dynamically create and manage residential property types.

Examples:

- Apartment Complex
- Rental House
- Condominium
- Townhouse
- Villa
- Hostel
- Student Residence
- Dormitory
- Gated Community
- Estate
- Duplex
- Triplex
- Serviced Apartments
- Senior Living Facility
- Mixed Residential Development

## Residential Unit Categories

Examples:

- Single Room
- Bedsitter
- Studio Apartment
- One Bedroom
- Two Bedroom
- Three Bedroom
- Four Bedroom
- Penthouse
- Maid's Room
- Family Unit
- Executive Suite

## Commercial Property Types

Administrators should be able to dynamically create and manage commercial property types.

Examples:

- Office Building
- Business Park
- Shopping Mall
- Retail Center
- Commercial Plaza
- Warehouse
- Industrial Park
- Factory
- Co-working Space
- Medical Center
- Hotel
- Conference Center
- Market Complex
- Fuel Station
- Mixed Commercial Development

## Commercial Unit Categories

Examples:

- Retail Shop
- Office Suite
- Executive Office
- Shared Office
- Warehouse Unit
- Storage Unit
- Restaurant Space
- Medical Office
- Banking Hall
- Showroom
- Kiosk
- Workshop
- Industrial Space

## Property Creation Workflow

When creating a property, the user must complete the classification hierarchy:

Property Category
    ├── Residential
    │     └── Property Type
    └── Commercial
          └── Property Type

Example:

Residential
    └── Apartment Complex
Commercial
    └── Shopping Mall
Residential
    └── Hostel

## Property Data Model

### Property Category

Required fields:

- Category Name
- Description
- Status
- Created By
- Created Date

### Property Type

Required fields:

- Category ID
- Property Type Name
- Description
- Status

Examples:

- Category: Residential | Type: Apartment Complex
- Category: Commercial | Type: Shopping Mall
- Category: Commercial | Type: Warehouse
- Category: Residential | Type: Hostel

