# Tenant Management Module

## Tenant Profile

Each tenant profile should store:

- Full Name
- National ID
- Passport Number
- Photo
- Phone
- Email
- Date of Birth
- Gender
- Marital Status
- Occupation
- Employer
- Work Address
- Emergency Contacts
- Guarantor Information
- Bank Details
- Preferred Payment Method
- Documents and Attachments
- Communication Preferences
- Tenant Type and Segment
- KYC Status
- Credit Score or Screening Results

## Tenant Lifecycle

The system should support:

- Tenant onboarding by property owners, managers, and agents
- Tenant self-registration from the mobile app and USSD interface
- KYC profile completion and verification before unit assignment
- Tenant verification and approval workflows
- Tenant assignment, revocation, reassignment, and transfer of units
- Eviction workflows
- Tenant exit and deposit reconciliation
- Tenant lease expiries and renewal management
- Tenant performance history and arrears tracking
- Exportable tenant lists and assignment history

## Tenant Onboarding Flows

Support:

- Property owners and property managers onboarding tenants directly through the web portal or admin console
- Tenant self-registration through the mobile app, tenant portal, or USSD flow with guided setup
- Multi-step onboarding workflows with document upload, identity verification, KYC checklist, and profile validation
- Optional tenant screening workflows including credit checks, background checks, employment validation, and guarantor approval
- Mandatory KYC completion before unit assignment, with configurable verification checkpoints, status gating, and escalation rules
- Approval gateways for owner review, leasing team sign-off, lease assignment, and unit allocation
- Automatic matching of approved tenant profiles to available units, lease products, and payment plans
- Integration with lease creation so onboarding flows transition seamlessly into billing, rent collection, and service charge setup
- Tenant onboarding dashboards with progress tracking, missing document alerts, and approval status visibility for administrators
- Tenant profile review and amendment workflows before final lease presentation
- Tenant welcome package generation with lease instructions, payment setup, access credentials, and move-in checklists
- Tenant data import and bulk onboarding support for CSV/Excel, partner portals, and corporate leasing programs
- Tenant list export to CSV/Excel and secure reports for compliance, board review, and audit purposes
- Onboarding templates and workflow presets for different tenant segments (residential, commercial, short-term, institutional)
- Communication workflows for welcome emails, verification reminders, document expiry alerts, and onboarding task notifications
- Audit logs for onboarding activity, profile changes, verification events, approvals, and user actions

---

# Lease Management

## Lease Creation

Lease agreements should support:

- Tenant
- Unit
- Property
- Lease Type
- Start Date
- End Date
- Lease Term and Termination Date
- Rent Amount
- Security Deposit
- Billing Cycle
- Payment Terms
- Late Payment Terms
- Notice Period
- Renewal Terms
- Rent Escalation
- Included Services
- Utility and Service Charge Allocation
- Deposits, Guarantees, and Insurance Requirements
- Penalties and Fees
- Lease Documents and Signatures
- Renewal Options and Break Clauses
- Tenant and Owner Obligations
- Subletting and Assignment Rules
- Early Termination Conditions
- Access and Entry Rights
- Dispute Resolution and Notice Contacts
- Lease-specific rules and custom conditions

## Lease Rules & Fees

Support:

- Penalties and fees defined as reusable rules with name, description, trigger, calculation method, and audit trail
- Late payment penalties based on fixed amounts, percentages, daily/weekly accrual, and tiered escalation
- Lease break penalties for early termination, abandonment, or improper notice
- Notice period rules for both tenant and landlord termination, renewal, and rent review
- Rent escalation rules by fixed amount, percentage, CPI/index-linked, step increases, or custom formulas
- Billing cycle adjustments for prorated rent, lease start mid-cycle, anniversary rent reviews, and rent-free periods
- Fee rules for administrative charges, dishonored payment fees, service charge penalties, legal fees, and inspection costs
- Automated calculation of penalty amounts and reconciliation against tenant ledger accounts
- Rule scoping by property, unit type, lease type, tenant segment, or regulatory jurisdiction
- Approval workflows for penalty application, fee waiver, and discretionary charge exceptions
- Audit logging of every rule application, override, and adjustment

## Billing Cycles

- Weekly
- Monthly
- Quarterly
- Semi Annual
- Annual
- Biweekly
- Custom billing cycle length
- Prorated interim billing for lease start/end transitions
- Consolidated billing across multiple leases for the same tenant or account
- Split-cycle billing for mixed lease terms

## Lease Workflows

Support:

- Lease approval with multi-step review, delegated approvals, and owner sign-off
- Lease renewal with automated renewal offers, tenant decision windows, and renewal reminders
- Lease termination with notice capture, inspection scheduling, move-out processing, and deposit reconciliation
- Early termination with break clause handling, penalty assessment, and notice validation
- Lease amendment for rent changes, service adjustments, lease extensions, and clause updates
- Renewal reminders with staged notifications, acceptance tracking, and renewal document generation
- Lease activation and hold workflows for provisional lease agreements
- Lease templates, clause libraries, and digital signature capture
- Lease anniversary and review reminders for rent escalation, contract renegotiation, and compliance checks
- Conditional workflow rules based on tenant type, lease value, property class, and approval thresholds
- Lease audit trail with change history, user comments, and version comparison
- Integration with document management for lease agreements, addenda, disclosures, and approvals

