# Non-Functional Requirements

## Scalability

- Support growth from small portfolios to enterprise estates with thousands of units and hundreds of tenants
- Scale database, API, and background processing independently
- Support horizontal scaling for web, mobile backend, and real-time services
- Support tenant-aware sharding, partitioning, or multi-tenant scaling strategies
- Provide capacity planning guidance and usage monitoring

## Security

- Secure authentication and authorization with RBAC and MFA
- Encrypt data in transit and at rest
- Strong password policies, session management, and token lifetimes
- Secure API access with rate limiting, input validation, and anti-CSRF controls
- Protect against common web/mobile vulnerabilities (OWASP Top 10)
- Audit logs for security events, access, and configuration changes
- Role-based access for property owners, managers, tenants, and support staff
- Data privacy and GDPR-style controls for personal information
- Secure key and secret management for infrastructure and integrations

## Performance

- Fast page load times and API response times under normal and peak usage
- Support concurrent users across web, mobile, and API clients
- Maintain performance for billing, reporting, and search queries
- Use caching and optimized queries for dashboards and frequent operations
- Monitor latency, throughput, and error rates

## Reliability

- Ensure predictable system behavior with high availability
- Support retry, backoff, and graceful degradation for external services
- Design fault-tolerant services for payments, notifications, and data storage
- Provide system health checks and self-healing deployment patterns
- Maintain consistent state across multi-step workflows such as lease creation and payment posting

## Availability

- Target high uptime for production deployments
- Plan for scheduled maintenance with notifications and minimal disruption
- Provide failover and recovery mechanisms for critical services
- Support disaster recovery with backup and restore procedures

## Usability

- Build intuitive workflows for property managers, owners, and tenants
- Provide clear onboarding, guided setup, and help content
- Support mobile-first, responsive design patterns
- Minimize required steps for common tasks
- Provide error handling with useful messaging and remediation steps

## Accessibility

- Conform to accessibility standards such as WCAG 2.1 AA where feasible
- Provide screen reader support, keyboard navigation, and accessible forms
- Ensure color contrast, text sizing, and UI clarity for all users
- Support accessibility features in mobile apps

## Internationalization and Localization

- Support multiple languages and region formats
- Localize currency, date, time, number, address, and phone formats
- Enable configurable locale settings per tenant or property
- Support translations for mobile and web interfaces

## Maintainability

- Modular architecture with clear separation of concerns
- Well-documented APIs, data models, and deployment processes
- Automated testing for unit, integration, and end-to-end workflows
- Code quality standards and linting for frontend and backend
- Maintain stable versioning and release management
- Provide operational runbooks and onboarding docs for support teams

## Extensibility

- Support plugin-like modules, configurable business rules, and feature flags
- Allow adding new payment methods, property types, and report templates
- Provide extension points for external integrations and custom workflows
- Design APIs and data schemas to support future features without broad refactoring

## Interoperability

- Use standard protocols (REST, GraphQL, WebSocket) for integration
- Support import/export via CSV, Excel, JSON, and APIs
- Provide webhook events for external systems
- Integrate with payment providers, messaging services, authentication providers, and third-party tools

## Observability and Monitoring

- Track application and infrastructure metrics, logs, and traces
- Monitor errors, performance, usage, and security incidents
- Provide alerting for critical failures, high latency, and payment issues
- Keep dashboards for business metrics such as occupancy, collections, and ticket backlog

## Data Management

- Define retention policies for lease, tenant, and accounting data
- Support secure backups, restore points, and archival storage
- Provide audit trails for financial transactions and configuration changes
- Ensure data consistency across tenant and property boundaries

## Compliance

- Support local regulatory and tax compliance requirements
- Provide configurable audit reporting and document retention
- Manage user consent and privacy disclosures
- Support KYC verification workflows and tenant identity checks

## Supportability

- Provide logs, diagnostics, and troubleshooting tools for administrators
- Include support workflows for tickets, complaints, and knowledge base management
- Design operations for automated deployment, rollback, and configuration management
- Enable tenant/owner administration and data export for audits

## Resilience

- Design for partial failure with isolated service faults
- Support graceful error handling for external dependency failures
- Maintain transactional consistency for payments, leases, and account balances
- Provide rollback or compensation actions for failed workflows

